jobs.description:
This is not your average production environment. The organisation you'll be joining is a global frontrunner in identity security, think biometric passports, secure payment cards, facial recognition at international airports, and cryptographic systems used by governments and banks worldwide. 

As Maintenance Engineer, you are the backbone of a smooth-running production floor. When machines go down, you're the one who gets things moving again, but more importantly, you make sure they don't go down in the first place. You combine hands-on technical skill with a structured mindset: you don't just fix problems, you prevent them. 

What you'll be doing

- Keeping production equipment in top condition and reducing unplanned downtime;
- Building and executing preventive maintenance schedules;
- Digging into the root cause of breakdowns — not just patching things up;
- Translating technical findings into clear documentation and practical improvement plans;
- Supporting the roll-out and commissioning of new equipment;
- Working with software controls for production machinery;
- Collaborating with production, management, and other departments on both day-to-day operations and longer-term reliability improvements;
- Monitoring facility and utility systems to ensure a safe working environment.

- An MBO level 4 background in Electrical or Manufacturing Engineering (or equivalent experience);
- A proven track record in a maintenance role within a production environment;
- Good command of English, spoken and written;
- Flexibility to work in shifts and join an on-call rotation;
- Willingness to occasionally travel for training or visits to other sites;
- Strong communication skills and a collaborative attitude.

Are you an avid cleaner or cleaner? Do you want to make sure that vacationing guests can start their vacation with a good feeling? Then read on quickly! 

We are looking for part-time cleaning employees for vacation park de Leistert in Roggel. Mondays and Fridays are the so-called changeover days when new guests arrive at the cottage. On these days it is important that the bungalows and vacation homes are cleaned properly. You do this with a whole team of enthusiastic and motivated cleaners. Together you make sure that everything looks spic and span. 

Tasks you will perform include:

- Making beds;
- Cleaning the kitchen, bathroom, bedroom and living room;
- Dusting and mopping everything; 
- Identifying defects and passing them on to the right people so that they can be repaired in a timely manner.

The work takes place on Mondays and Fridays between 9 a.m. and 3 p.m. Would you like to work more? Please let us know so we can discuss the possibilities! 

- You are a motivated cleaner who knows how to get things done;
- You speak the Dutch, English or German language;
- It is no problem to come to the location in Roggel (public transport is also possible); 
- You are available at least on Mondays and Fridays.

In the vacation periods it is always extra busy, it is important that you are flexible in these periods!

Are you a hands-on worker, do you like working in an organized way, and do you feel at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to be part of one of Europe’s largest producers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position at our client in Waalwijk is perfect for you!

As a Logistics Employee, you play an important role in the logistics process surrounding the production of high-quality, custom-made sandwich panels for, among others, the bodywork industry and the defense sector. You ensure that materials, raw materials, and finished products are available at the right place and at the right time.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, in a close-knit team of colleagues. Order, overview, and safety are central to your daily tasks.

As a Logistics Employee, your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading goods using a forklift;

- Receiving and assisting drivers (first point of contact);

- Packing and preparing finished products for shipment;

- Managing internal logistics between the warehouse and production departments;

- Supplying raw materials to various production departments;

- Cleaning and organizing the warehouse and production halls;

- Ensuring a safe and tidy workplace.

Requirements

- You work in a structured manner and have an eye for order and safety;

- You hold a valid forklift certificate;

- You are a true team player;

- You have a good command of the Dutch or English language.

Looking for a stable job with great pay and opportunities to grow?

Do you enjoy staying active and working as part of a team? Whether you already have experience in logistics or are looking for a fresh start, DHL gives you the opportunity to learn, develop, and build your career.

As a Warehouse Employee, you will help ensure that customer orders are processed and shipped on time. Together with your colleagues, you play an important role in keeping one of DHL's largest logistics operations running smoothly.

Experience in logistics is not required. We value your motivation, commitment, and work ethic above everything else.

In addition:

- You are available for day, evening, and night shifts;
- You enjoy physical work;
- You have your own transportation;
- You are a team player;
- You speak and understand English.

Are you experienced in a warehouse and ready to take the next step into a leadership role? Or do you already have some experience in supervising colleagues and want to further develop yourself as a team leader? Then this is your opportunity! Within a fast-growing and international logistics environment, you will have the opportunity to further develop your leadership skills and  take on more responsibility step by step.

As a (junior) Warehouse Team Leader, you will work alongside an experienced team and supervise a group of 10 to 12 employees. You will be visibly present on the work floor, supporting the daily coordination of operations. You work closely with the Supervisor and be given the space to grow in your role.

Your responsibilities include:

- Supporting the supervision and guidance of warehouse employees;
- Working on the floor to ensure smooth daily operations;
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and discussing them with your manager;
- Contributing to the improvement of work processes;
- Monitoring basic safety and quality regulations;
- Working with simple reports and developing basic Excel skills.

We are primarily looking for someone with the right motivation and ambition to grow into a leadership role within logistics. In addition, you have:

- Experience in a warehouse or logistics environment;
- Interest in supervising or guiding colleagues;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Basic knowledge of Excel or willingness to learn;
- A proactive and eager-to-learn attitude;
- Availability to work full-time in a two-shift system.

Have you not yet held a full team leader position, but do you have ambition and some initial experience in leading others? We strongly encourage you to apply.

Are you passionate about quality, compliance and continuous improvement?Do you enjoy optimizing processes and ensuring that quality standards are maintained throughout an organization? Then this position as Quality Specialist could be the perfect next step in your career.

What will you do?

As a Quality Specialist, you will be responsible for managing, maintaining and continuously improving the Quality Management System (QMS). You will support site management, ensure compliance with customer and regulatory requirements, and help create a strong quality culture across the organization.

Your responsibilities include:

- Planning, implementing and maintaining the Quality Management System (QMS);
- Ensuring quality governance and compliance across logistics operations;
- Promoting a strong culture of quality and continuous improvement;
- Coordinating internal and external audits and following up on improvement actions;
- Monitoring customer, legal and third-party quality requirements;
- Identifying improvement opportunities and supporting process optimization;
- Advising and supporting management and operational teams on quality-related matters.

What do you bring?

- Proven experience in quality management within a logistics or operational environment;
- Knowledge of Quality Management Systems (QMS) and audit methodologies;
- Experience with compliance and continuous improvement;
- Strong analytical and communication skills;
- A proactive, structured and detail-oriented mindset;
- Good command of the English language.
